# Phase 3: Build AI & Matching Engine

## Overview

Replace keyword matching with AI-powered analysis. GPT-4o-mini analyzes product → generates personalized channel recommendations + copy-paste outreach scripts per channel. This is the VALUE MULTIPLIER that justifies payment.

## Requirements

- Functional: AI generates product analysis + per-channel outreach scripts personalized to product
- Non-functional: <10s total response time, <$0.01 per analysis (GPT-4o-mini cost), cache results

## Architecture

```
ProductProfile (from scraper)
  → GPT-4o-mini: "Analyze this product. Who is the target user?"
  → Enhanced ProductProfile with: target_persona, value_prop, unique_angle
  → Channel Matching (semantic, not just keyword)
  → Per-channel: GPT-4o-mini generates outreach script
  → Cache result in Turso DB
  → Return full report
```

## Related Code Files

- Create: `src/ai-analyzer.ts` — Product analysis via OpenAI
- Create: `src/script-generator.ts` — Per-channel outreach script generation
- Create: `src/db.ts` — Turso/SQLite connection + schema
- Modify: `src/channels.ts` — Add semantic matching
- Modify: `src/index.ts` — Wire AI into analysis pipeline

## Implementation Steps

### Step 1: Database Setup (2h)

1. Set up Turso database (free tier):
   ```sql
   CREATE TABLE analyses (
     id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
     url TEXT NOT NULL,
     product_profile JSON,
     ai_analysis JSON,
     channels JSON,
     scripts JSON,
     created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
   );
   
   CREATE TABLE users (
     id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
     email TEXT,
     stripe_customer_id TEXT,
     plan TEXT DEFAULT 'free',
     analyses_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
     created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
   );
   ```

2. Cache layer: same URL analyzed within 24h → return cached result

### Step 2: AI Product Analyzer (4h)

3. Build prompt for product analysis:
   ```
   System: You are a distribution strategist for indie software products.
   
   Given this product info:
   - Title: {title}
   - Description: {description}
   - Features: {features}
   - Pricing: {pricing}
   
   Analyze and return JSON:
   {
     "target_persona": "Who exactly would use this?",
     "pain_point": "What specific problem does it solve?",
     "value_prop": "Why this over alternatives?",
     "unique_angle": "What's the hook for cold outreach?",
     "category": "saas|api|marketplace|extension|template|content",
     "keywords": ["5-10 relevant keywords for channel matching"]
   }
   ```

4. Use GPT-4o-mini for cost efficiency (~$0.002 per analysis)
5. Parse response, validate JSON, fallback to keyword matching if AI fails

### Step 3: Semantic Channel Matching (4h)

6. Enhanced matching algorithm:
   ```
   Score = (keyword_overlap × 0.3) + (category_match × 0.3) + 
           (audience_relevance × 0.2) + (commercial_tolerance × 0.2)
   ```

7. Add "anti-match" rules:
   - r/SaaS: only if product IS SaaS
   - r/webdev: only if product targets developers
   - Facebook groups: only if product serves non-tech users
   - HN: only if product has technical novelty

8. Return top 15 channels, ordered by expected conversion (not just audience size)

### Step 4: Script Generator (3h)

9. Per-channel outreach script generation:
   ```
   System: Write a {platform}-appropriate post/message for this product.
   
   Product: {ai_analysis}
   Channel: {channel_name} on {platform}
   Channel rules: {dont_do}
   Best format: {best_format}
   
   Requirements:
   - Value-first (lead with insight, not pitch)
   - Under 150 words
   - Include specific hook for THIS community
   - End with soft CTA (ask for feedback, not "buy now")
   ```

10. Generate scripts for top 10 channels (batch API call)
11. Include "What NOT to do" warning per channel

### Step 5: Wire Together + Deploy (2h)

12. Update analysis endpoint:
    - Free: product analysis + top 5 channels (no scripts)
    - Paid: full 15 channels + AI scripts + "What NOT to do" + timing recs
13. Deploy to Cloudflare Workers with Turso binding
14. Test with 20 real product URLs

## Success Criteria

- [ ] AI product analysis returns valid JSON for 18/20 test URLs
- [ ] Semantic matching produces more relevant results than keyword-only (A/B comparison)
- [ ] Scripts are personalized and channel-appropriate (manual QA: 7/10 quality)
- [ ] Total cost per analysis <$0.01
- [ ] Response time <10s for full analysis
- [ ] Results cached in Turso, cache hit returns <1s
- [ ] Free vs paid tier gating works correctly

## Risk Assessment

| Risk | Probability | Mitigation |
|------|-------------|------------|
| OpenAI API costs spike | 15% | GPT-4o-mini is cheap; add rate limit 100 analyses/day |
| AI generates bad scripts | 25% | Add manual review for first 50 analyses; iterate prompt |
| Turso free tier limits | 10% | 9GB storage, 500M rows read/mo — plenty for MVP |
| AI hallucinations in product analysis | 20% | Always show scraped data alongside AI interpretation |
